Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.01,0:05:30.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Not even a clue.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.03,0:05:33.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you been able to\Ncome up with anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.29,0:05:35.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.20,0:05:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,There are nine million\Npeople in Cairo alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.09,0:05:40.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no idea how many buildings\Nare out there similar to this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.81,0:05:44.31,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way we can find it\Nby this friggin' picture alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.39,0:05:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's Jotaro?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.61,0:05:47.91,Default,,0,0,0,,He is in a cafe down the road with Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.03,0:05:48.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Joestar.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.57,0:05:53.97,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.53,0:05:55.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa! Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.67,0:05:59.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.58,0:06:01.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Shouldn't you be tamed by now? Jeez!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.59,0:06:14.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What? Right. Mm-hmm. Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.97,0:06:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.51,0:06:26.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid the situation has\Nbecome most urgent now. Miss Holly?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.51,0:06:29.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I was just told that she\Nlapsed into a coma last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.55,0:06:33.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet we still don't have many\Nclues as to Dio's whereabouts.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.17,0:06:36.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Has the Speedwagon Foundation\Nbeen able to find out anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.35,0:06:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Still no information\Nfrom them. In addition,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.29,0:06:43.53,Default,,0,0,0,,my psychography stopped working just after\NI mentally photographed this mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.61,0:06:46.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Some kind of psychic\Nbarrier may be in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.93,0:06:47.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.05,0:06:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, just waiting around\Nhere won't solve the problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.37,0:06:53.01,Default,,0,0,0,,We should do everything we can.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.09,0:06:53.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.35,0:06:56.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, excuse me, but we're\Nlooking for this building.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.03,0:06:58.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know where this is?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.13,0:07:01.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I know you're a visitor,\Nbut I'm trying to run a cafe here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.11,0:07:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,So could you and your\Nfriends order something?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.33,0:07:05.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, right. Sorry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.73,0:07:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll have four iced teas.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.33,0:07:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, can't help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.51,0:07:25.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.45,0:07:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll ask somewhere else.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.83,0:07:28.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm familiar with that building.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.11,0:07:31.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.02,0:07:33.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I'm quite certain of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.89,0:07:36.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You there, did you just\Nsay you know about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.31,0:07:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir, I did. You do? Really now?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.55,0:07:42.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What great luck! Thank goodness.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.55,0:07:44.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, tell me, where is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.11,0:07:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Ain't this information\Nworth something to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.61,0:07:53.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, right you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.05,0:07:56.17,Default,,0,0,0,,My apologies, and here's ten pounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.33,0:07:57.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, please, tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.55,0:08:01.89,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, sir, I just love to gamble.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.17,0:08:05.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a sucker for a cheap thrill, and\NI can't seem to stay away from it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.87,0:08:09.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Heck, truth be known, I make my\Nliving on games of luck and skill.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.49,0:08:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way, sir, do you\Never engage in gambling?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.25,0:08:15.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't understand where\Nyou're going with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.69,0:08:18.67,Default,,0,0,0,,If you don't care for gambling,\Nwhy don't you just say so?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.75,0:08:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Look here, I'm asking you where\Nyou're going with all this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.33,0:08:25.07,Default,,0,0,0,,What I'm saying is, would you like to bet\Nagainst me in a little game of chance?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.15,0:08:27.67,Default,,0,0,0,,If you win, I'll tell you\Nwhat you want to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.75,0:08:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Free, of course. A bet?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.79,0:08:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm good at winning bets, but we\Nreally have no time for poker games.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.53,0:08:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I'll pay you 20 pounds more,\Nso please, tell me where it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.59,0:08:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.65,0:08:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,A bag can be made over any little thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.97,0:08:42.65,Default,,0,0,0,,For example, take a look\Nat that wall over yonder.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.73,0:08:43.85,Default,,0,0,0,,See that cat there?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.07,0:08:47.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Now then,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.98,0:08:51.90,Default,,0,0,0,,why don't we just bet on which piece of\Nbeef jerky that cat will go after first?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.99,0:08:53.53,Default,,0,0,0,,The left one or the right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.01,0:08:54.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Come now, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.19,0:08:57.07,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to admit this is exciting.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.15,0:08:58.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen up and don't be a jerk.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.15,0:09:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Just take the 30 pounds\Nand tell us what you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.71,0:09:04.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Polnareff, you should watch your mouth\Nwhen you're asking someone for a favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.85,0:09:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.97,0:09:07.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take your stinking bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.31,0:09:08.60,Default,,0,0,0,,The cat will go right!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.99,0:09:09.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.90,0:09:11.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Now this is getting interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.41,0:09:13.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take the one on the left, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.39,0:09:14.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.31,0:09:17.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro, don't you think he is suspicious?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.67,0:09:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.58,0:09:22.87,Default,,0,0,0,,If he makes any strange moves,\Nattack him. Immediately. I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.81,0:09:26.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, that cat can smell the jerky now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.05,0:09:31.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, and, uh, by the way, what is\Nit I have to pay you if I lose?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.77,0:09:32.97,Default,,0,0,0,,About a hundred pounds?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.05,0:09:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,No, no money.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.85,0:09:36.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's play for something more interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.01,0:09:37.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Your soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.43,0:09:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.43,0:09:41.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Jerking us around, this bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.53,0:09:42.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Accept the bet, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.47,0:09:46.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Your soul it is. Here he comes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.53,0:09:47.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on to your dog now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.11,0:09:51.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like the kitty's going to the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.05,0:09:56.09,Default,,0,0,0,,If I were that cat, I would\Ngo for the bigger piece.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.17,0:09:57.99,Default,,0,0,0,,And the right one looks bigger.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.99,0:10:03.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.90,0:10:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you see that it went\Nfor the one on the left
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.09,0:10:08.95,Default,,0,0,0,,first so I won now what\Nare you going to do you're
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.03,0:10:11.29,Default,,0,0,0,,only making it more difficult\Nto ask for the location
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.37,0:10:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,of the building now since\Nyou lost that little game
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.25,0:10:17.85,Default,,0,0,0,,it's time for you to pay\Nup huh pay you with what
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.93,0:10:21.47,Default,,0,0,0,,now sir don't try to welch\Non me now I want to soul
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.55,0:10:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,you bet you see I'm a stand\Nuser who collects souls
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.71,0:10:27.69,Default,,0,0,0,,the gambling makes them\Nthat much easier to extract.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.77,0:10:30.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I strike when defeat\Nmakes a man vulnerable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.83,0:10:35.99,Default,,0,0,0,,What? Polnareff!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.21,0:10:37.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid it's too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.13,0:10:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,And if I die, Polnareff's\Nsoul goes with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.93,0:10:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,So, you best not attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.51,0:10:45.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Polnareff!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.73,0:10:48.89,Default,,0,0,0,,No pulse.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.21,0:10:50.07,Default,,0,0,0,,He's dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.33,0:10:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,The name is Darby.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.77,0:10:56.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Daniel J. Darby.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.73,0:10:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, and by the way, this here is my cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.25,0:11:01.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.63,0:11:06.53,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Polnareff's soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.97,0:11:10.09,Default,,0,0,0,,With this, I've eliminated\None of Lord Dio's enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.33,0:11:12.65,Default,,0,0,0,,A very foolish one, I might add.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.15,0:11:17.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Bastard! How dare you! Bedding?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.99,0:11:20.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That cat over there belongs to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.11,0:11:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,That is called cheating.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.87,0:11:22.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheating?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.78,0:11:27.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, sir, if you can't see through a\Nsimple trick, ain't that your own fault?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.39,0:11:29.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, to me, gambling is a relationship.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.97,0:11:32.43,Default,,0,0,0,,If you think of it as a\Nrelationship of deceit,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.51,0:11:35.92,Default,,0,0,0,,then the one who cries first\Nis the loser, you understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.25,0:11:40.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Sir, I get the distinct impression you'd\Nlike to kill me with your bare hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.19,0:11:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But what about your friends, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.31,0:11:46.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, don't think we are just\Ngoing to let you get away with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.61,0:11:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,September 22nd, 1984,\Nat exactly 11.15 p.m.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.85,0:11:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Do y 'all happen to remember\Nwhat you were doing right then?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.25,0:11:55.09,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.17,0:11:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.33,0:12:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,At the time, I was gambling with a man\Ncalled Stephen Moore in California.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.67,0:12:04.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I mentioned it because he told me\Nthe exact same thing you just said.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.61,0:12:06.35,Default,,0,0,0,,That man is now this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.85,0:12:10.69,Default,,0,0,0,,The one below is Moore's father,\Nand the one next to him is his wife.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.77,0:12:13.45,Default,,0,0,0,,As you can see, if you\Nwant Polnareff's soul back,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.53,0:12:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,you have no choice but to continue.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.21,0:12:16.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Gamble it with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.77,0:12:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,This man is a devil.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.09,0:12:22.87,Default,,0,0,0,,This guy's trying to take us one by one!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.75,0:12:29.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, gents, are you gonna\Ncash in your chips or what?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.05,0:12:31.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.49,0:12:32.95,Default,,0,0,0,,why don't you have a drink and think it
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.03,0:12:35.23,Default,,0,0,0,,over may I offer you
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.31,0:12:41.99,Default,,0,0,0,,some chocolate mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.19,0:12:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Joestar what is it
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.53,0:12:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,you are doing there.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.44,0:12:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Right then.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.35,0:12:51.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know what surface\Ntension is Barbie my boy?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.33,0:12:52.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Darby sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.65,0:12:53.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The name is Darby.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.03,0:12:56.63,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the molecular attraction\Nacting on the surface
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.71,0:12:58.95,Default,,0,0,0,,of that liquor allowing it\Nto swell without spilling.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.03,0:13:00.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this a game?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.53,0:13:01.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The rules are simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.91,0:13:03.50,Default,,0,0,0,,We will take turns dropping
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.71,0:13:07.79,Default,,0,0,0,,coins into this glass and you lose\Nwhen the liquor spills over the edge.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.87,0:13:08.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey old man.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.97,0:13:10.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You You cannot do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.11,0:13:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I hereby bet my soul. Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.13,0:13:14.97,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you cannot do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.17,0:13:16.81,Default,,0,0,0,,This man is a dirty cheat.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.95,0:13:18.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't let him cheat.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.25,0:13:20.57,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I chose the nature of the bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.65,0:13:22.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro, keep an eye on him.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.91,0:13:23.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.93,0:13:27.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But before we begin, I should like\Nto inspect those coins in this glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.77,0:13:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You're well within your rights, but\Nthere's something I need to ask.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.13,0:13:34.79,Default,,0,0,0,,What's our guarantee that Polnareff's\Nsoul will be returned if you lose?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.87,0:13:36.95,Default,,0,0,0,,If I lose, his soul will return.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.25,0:13:39.84,Default,,0,0,0,,It's within my stand's\Nabilities to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.01,0:13:43.13,Default,,0,0,0,,My pride as a gambler is all\Nthe guarantee you need, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.21,0:13:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,And what makes you think I'm foolish\Nenough just to take your word on that?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.81,0:13:49.40,Default,,0,0,0,,When engaged in gambling,\Npeople take risks.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.53,0:13:51.41,Default,,0,0,0,,They must pay for their actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.61,0:13:55.17,Default,,0,0,0,,By collecting the souls of others,\NI'm risking my own life as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.25,0:13:57.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I wouldn't lie by my own wager.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.53,0:13:58.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Right then.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.44,0:14:00.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You go first. Mr. Joestar!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.39,0:14:01.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Just trust me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.67,0:14:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, sir, may I drop in any\Nnumber of coins that I wish?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.87,0:14:08.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Go ahead, as long as you\Ndrop them all in at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.77,0:14:10.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Five. Five coins.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.17,0:14:13.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Quiet down, and y 'all\Nplease don't touch the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.93,0:14:24.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Now it's your turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.37,0:14:27.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You have nerves of steel to\Ndrop in five coins at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.65,0:14:31.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Well now, I think I'll just play\Nit safe and stick in one coin.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.81,0:14:36.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The old man, he's adding\Nmore liquor to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.15,0:14:38.31,Default,,0,0,0,,And he tells me to keep an\Neye out for any cheating.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.39,0:14:41.19,Default,,0,0,0,,What a hustler and a\Ndamn good one at that!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.07,0:14:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way you can get\Nany more coins in there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.33,0:14:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, you're the one that\Nsaid that cheating is okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.65,0:14:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless you're caught.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.59,0:14:58.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Whoa, I was really sweating.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.41,0:15:00.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought it was going\Nto spill over for sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.27,0:15:02.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now it's your turn, Orby, my boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.41,0:15:07.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Darby!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.32,0:15:09.84,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll thank you not to\Nmake that mistake again, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.93,0:15:10.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Darby!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.84,0:15:11.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Not Orby or Barbie!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.15,0:15:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, sorry about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.05,0:15:15.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Thought he had me for a moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.35,0:15:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Now he's getting the guy bent out of shape\Nby mispronouncing his name on purpose.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.95,0:15:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,The old man's gotta be\Na natural-born gambler.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.99,0:15:24.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, Darby, shall we\Ncontinue with our bet?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.93,0:15:25.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It's your turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.55,0:15:29.32,Default,,0,0,0,,The shadow's blocking my line.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.75,0:15:31.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like to drop it in from over here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.15,0:15:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Perfectly fine with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.73,0:15:36.15,Default,,0,0,0,,In any case, the surface\Ntension has reached its limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.23,0:15:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The merest touch will cause it to spill.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.93,0:15:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'm sure you must be\Nthinking, it's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.07,0:15:46.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The surface tension has reached its limit.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.31,0:15:47.14,Default,,0,0,0,,But you know what?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.22,0:15:48.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You're wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.77,0:15:56.83,Default,,0,0,0,,That's impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.03,0:15:58.53,Default,,0,0,0,,It has to spill over the edge!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.61,0:16:01.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, what do you mean\Nit has to spill over?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.43,0:16:02.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Y 'all saw me, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.55,0:16:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I dropped that coin in, so\Nit's your turn, Mr. Joestar.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.77,0:16:11.81,Default,,0,0,0,,He didn't make any funny moves\Nlike he was trying to cheat.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.89,0:16:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I was watching him with Star Platinum.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.79,0:16:16.49,Default,,0,0,0,,He just dropped in all\Nthe coins nice and clean.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.57,0:16:17.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.15,0:16:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It was perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.61,0:16:23.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I planned it perfectly so it would\Nspill over on the very next coin.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.67,0:16:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Why didn't it? Hurry up, Mr. Joestar.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.95,0:16:29.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Y 'all ain't waitin' for that\Nliquor to dry up, are ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.07,0:16:32.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I... I...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.07,0:16:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.77,0:16:35.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Joestar!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.59,0:16:42.13,Default,,0,0,0,,In his mind, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.29,0:16:44.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Joestar's already admitted his defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.43,0:16:46.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why his soul was expelled.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.55,0:16:48.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Once again, I have won the bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.03,0:16:53.23,Default,,0,0,0,,That's two chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.57,0:16:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's continue gambling.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.77,0:16:58.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless you're planning to run away\Nand leave these poor folks behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.73,0:16:59.61,Default,,0,0,0,,You bastard!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.55,0:17:01.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop it now, Avdol.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.15,0:17:04.03,Default,,0,0,0,,So you still don't get it, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.11,0:17:07.11,Default,,0,0,0,,If you kill me, both of\Ntheir souls perish as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.53,0:17:08.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Shit.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.07,0:17:10.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what's going on over here?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.71,0:17:12.33,Default,,0,0,0,,If you want to make\Ntrouble, take it outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.41,0:17:14.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Shut up and mind your own business.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.87,0:17:24.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Well done, but too late. Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.27,0:17:27.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Is there something wrong\Nwith that glass, Jotaro?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.67,0:17:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,A piece of melted chocolate\Nis on the bottom of the glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.55,0:17:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He must have stuck it\Non while inspecting the
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.67,0:17:34.89,Default,,0,0,0,,glass and coins at the\Nbeginning of the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.97,0:17:36.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought we had to understand it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.67,0:17:39.21,Default,,0,0,0,,A cheater is not a cheater\Nunless he gets caught.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.29,0:17:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.41,0:17:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,How can a piece of chocolate allow\Nmore coins to be dropped in the glass?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.91,0:17:45.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Although it's melted now,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.09,0:17:47.49,Default,,0,0,0,,when he first put the chocolate\Non the glass, it was solid,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.57,0:17:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,so it tipped the glass slightly, making\Nthe liquor appear filled to the brim.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.09,0:17:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,When the chocolate melted, it could no\Nlonger support the weight of the glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.29,0:17:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,The glass leveled out slowly,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.97,0:17:59.95,Default,,0,0,0,,lowering the level of the liquor and\Nallowing just enough room for one more coin.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.03,0:18:00.86,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.94,0:18:03.92,Default,,0,0,0,,But how could he make the chocolate\Nmelt during his turn instead of Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.01,0:18:04.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Joestar's?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.15,0:18:06.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The heat from the sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.91,0:18:10.68,Default,,0,0,0,,He protected the glass from direct\Nsunlight with his own shadow.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.79,0:18:13.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, when he changed\Npositions, the chocolate melted.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.57,0:18:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Darby, get your cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.95,0:18:23.53,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll settle this once\Nand for all with poker.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.61,0:18:24.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.63,0:18:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I consider poker to be my strongest\Ngame, so this should be interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.71,0:18:30.55,Default,,0,0,0,,A poker game?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.65,0:18:33.85,Default,,0,0,0,,But this guy even beat\NMr. Joestar! I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.15,0:18:35.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Even though he doesn't use force,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.07,0:18:39.48,Default,,0,0,0,,he's the most dangerous stand\Nuser we've ever come across.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.55,0:18:41.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But it doesn't matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.91,0:18:43.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't back out of this one.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.59,0:18:45.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Before we start, let's try something.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.23,0:18:47.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Shuffle those cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.97,0:18:48.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.19,0:18:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you up to, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.41,0:18:55.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Pick a card, any card you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.87,0:18:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Just don't let me see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.15,0:19:01.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me take a guess.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.47,0:19:02.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Six of hearts.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.19,0:19:06.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll read the cards in\Norder, starting from the top.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.35,0:19:10.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Five of spades, queen of diamonds,\Njack of spades, ace of hearts,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.51,0:19:13.28,Default,,0,0,0,,seven of diamonds, six\Nof clubs, king of clubs.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.49,0:19:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.40,0:19:15.32,Default,,0,0,0,,You guessed them all?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.41,0:19:18.41,Default,,0,0,0,,But Darby, he shuffled\Nthe cards. How did you...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.49,0:19:20.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I can tell you all the cards in order.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.81,0:19:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Star Platinum's eyes caught everything\Nyou did and saw where every card went.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.37,0:19:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a very interesting parlor trick.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.45,0:19:29.49,Default,,0,0,0,,But all it means is\Nthat I have to keep the
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.57,0:19:31.59,Default,,0,0,0,,cards hidden from view\Nwhile I shuffle them,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.67,0:19:32.50,Default,,0,0,0,,doesn't it, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.58,0:19:33.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you get it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.89,0:19:38.35,Default,,0,0,0,,What I'm telling you is it's not going to\Nbe so easy for you to cheat from now on.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.43,0:19:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Just a little friendly warning.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.59,0:19:42.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.79,0:19:44.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's a fresh deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.23,0:19:45.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Factory sealed.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.37,0:19:48.89,Default,,0,0,0,,It includes one Joker.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.23,0:19:50.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like a standard deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.79,0:19:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.70,0:19:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's start the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.27,0:19:55.63,Default,,0,0,0,,The Ten of Hearts.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.13,0:19:57.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Seven of Clubs.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.73,0:19:59.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That makes me the dealer.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.85,0:20:01.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess I better shuffle\Nthe cards somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.87,0:20:03.11,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't see them, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.19,0:20:04.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Kindly cut the deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.65,0:20:25.49,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing, Star\NPlatinum? Just broke.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.57,0:20:28.15,Default,,0,0,0,,darby's finger why did\Nyou do that i warned you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.23,0:20:30.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not going to overlook\Nany cheating from
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.45,0:20:33.11,Default,,0,0,0,,now on cheating when i\Ndid not see him make any?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.19,0:20:35.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Suspicious moves look\Ncarefully at those cards
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.99,0:20:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,he's got in his hand the\Nsecond card from the top!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.57,0:20:42.63,Default,,0,0,0,,That's Hanged is the card he tried to\Ndeal to me just now. He pretended to
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.71,0:20:46.27,Default,,0,0,0,,deal the cards in order From the top\Nbut actually intended to deal me the
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.35,0:20:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,second card so the card on top would\Nhave gone to Him giving him a winning
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.09,0:20:57.31,Default,,0,0,0,,hand of three of a kind you're brutal\Nman you broke my finger on the contrary.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.39,0:20:58.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Mary, I'm full of mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.77,0:21:00.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I could have severed your finger.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.19,0:21:02.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.10,0:21:04.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheating takes advantage of\Npsychological blind spots.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.17,0:21:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Having good vision ain't\Nenough to catch cheating.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.49,0:21:10.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't expect you to\Nsee me deal in seconds.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.23,0:21:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take this lesson to heart and\Nwon't underestimate anyone again.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.29,0:21:17.29,Default,,0,0,0,,This finger will be accepted\Nas a reminder of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.55,0:21:22.31,Default,,0,0,0,,But, Jotaro, I'm not here to\Nfight for Lord Dio. No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.47,0:21:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I came here to fight because\NI'm a born gambling man.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.63,0:21:29.22,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'm going to challenge you\Nwith all my strength and soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.67,0:21:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I've split each one of\Ntheir souls into six chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.47,0:21:41.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Poker is the type of gambling\Ngame that allows you to
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.85,0:21:44.23,Default,,0,0,0,,quit when you know you'll\Nlose it against your opponent.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.31,0:21:48.91,Default,,0,0,0,,But because you have to pay for each turn,\Ntwo chips are not enough to play a game.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.99,0:21:50.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Three is the minimum.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.61,0:21:54.67,Default,,0,0,0,,A soul is returned only after you\Nwin all six chips back, understood?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.87,0:21:56.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.78,0:21:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like to offer you\Nsome chips if y 'all still
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.63,0:22:00.87,Default,,0,0,0,,willing to engage in\Nthis here gambling game,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.95,0:22:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,but I need to hear y 'all\Nsay those little words.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.45,0:22:05.83,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, I will bet my soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.01,0:22:07.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.91,0:22:09.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro! Well,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.25,0:22:12.49,Default,,0,0,0,,since you can't shuffle\Nwith that hand of yours,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.57,0:22:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,why don't we get a third\Nparty to do it for us?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:15.97,0:22:18.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Abdul, let's ask that kid\Non the hill over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.45,0:22:20.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Bring him here. Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.81,0:22:26.21,Default,,0,0,0,,This here stack of Snow White chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.51,0:22:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,They represent your immortal soul, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.09,0:22:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,When I take all six of them, I will\Nadd your soul to my collection.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.63,0:22:39.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry, we need you to\Ndo this for us. Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.83,0:22:47.39,Default,,0,0,0,,As for the ante, one little Polnareff.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.51,0:22:50.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.13,0:22:57.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, let's see now.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.69,0:22:59.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take two cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.37,0:23:00.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Give me three.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.57,0:23:04.47,Default,,0,0,0,,My, my.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.55,0:23:05.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Just look at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.85,0:23:07.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Seems you got a good hand, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.71,0:23:08.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see how it goes?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.62,0:23:11.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll raise one Polnareff\Nfor the time being!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.69,0:23:12.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Same here!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.60,0:23:14.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless he folds?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.23,0:23:16.37,Default,,0,0,0,,At least three chips are needed per hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.45,0:23:17.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I call.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.87,0:23:18.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Show me your hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.73,0:23:22.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Two pair, eights and nines. Sorry, bud.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.01,0:23:24.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Two pair, queens or jacks?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.13,0:23:27.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodness on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.87,0:23:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I almost went and lost this here game.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.23,0:23:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Three chips left.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.75,0:23:34.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's go on to the next hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.53,0:23:35.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Deal the cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.44,0:23:36.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, another game.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.07,0:23:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I sure hope it won't\Nbe your last game, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.01,0:23:48.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take one.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.85,0:23:52.91,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.27,0:23:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry up and look at your cards, so you\Ncan decide if you're going to draw a fold.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.05,0:23:58.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I've decided that I'm going to hold.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.95,0:23:59.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.29,0:24:02.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, could you kindly repeat that, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:02.95,0:24:04.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure I must have heard you wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.91,0:24:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You're saying you're keeping them?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.01,0:24:08.11,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what I said.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.19,0:24:09.02,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm keeping them.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.10,0:24:11.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to bet with\Nthese five cards. I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.27,0:24:14.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I know you just want to\Nhold on to your cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.97,0:24:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,But why didn't you look at them first?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.91,0:24:17.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll keep them.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.91,0:24:20.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Answer my question, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.63,0:24:23.47,Default,,0,0,0,,How can you play the game\Nwithout looking at your cards?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.55,0:24:25.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, kid, don't worry about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.15,0:24:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Just stay calm and deal\Nthe cards, all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.13,0:24:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.04,0:24:32.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Avdol, I need a favor. A favor?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.35,0:24:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll go along with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.81,0:24:36.85,Default,,0,0,0,,But why aren't you looking at your cards?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.93,0:24:38.75,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare you ignore me like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.83,0:24:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I demand that you answer me!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:40.47,0:24:42.47,Default,,0,0,0,,In addition to my remaining chips,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.43,0:24:47.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to raise you all\Nof Avdol's soul. Huh? What?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.59,0:24:52.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Darby, you are a very cool-headed man.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:52.61,0:24:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You take careful, calculated actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.15,0:24:58.33,Default,,0,0,0,,You do not use force, yet\Nyou are a very powerful man.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.73,0:25:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,My personality is not suited for gambling.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.25,0:25:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm the type to lose my temper too easily.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:03.45,0:25:06.03,Default,,0,0,0,,If I play against you, I\Nwill most certainly lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.11,0:25:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,But I believe in Jotaro.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.05,0:25:11.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not yet understand his reasons\Nfor leaving those cards face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:11.51,0:25:15.39,Default,,0,0,0,,But if Jotaro wants me to\Nbet, I will trust him and bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.33,0:25:19.27,Default,,0,0,0,,My soul, or whatever else it may take!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.15,0:25:23.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Well now,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:23.55,0:25:25.51,Default,,0,0,0,,it appears you gentlemen\Nare taking leave of
Dialogue: 0,0:25:25.59,0:25:27.85,Default,,0,0,0,,your senses from the\Npressure of this game.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.93,0:25:28.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.84,0:25:30.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I asked you for a card, boy!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.49,0:25:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Now hurry up! Uh, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:34.97,0:25:35.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.88,0:25:37.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Darby, I did as you asked.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.65,0:25:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I dealt him a bum hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.49,0:25:40.67,Default,,0,0,0,,This man is nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:41.59,0:25:43.91,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no mistake. I'm certain.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.93,0:25:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro may think he chose\Nsome innocent child, but I,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.37,0:25:52.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Darby, owned this here shop and\Neveryone within a stone's throw of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:52.25,0:25:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter who he chooses to deal,\Nthe results will be the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.73,0:25:57.97,Default,,0,0,0,,His cards will be nothing but garbage.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:58.31,0:26:01.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Betting without looking at\Nhis cards, he's bluffing.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:01.53,0:26:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare you bluff against me?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.37,0:26:06.08,Default,,0,0,0,,What makes you think I'm\Ngonna fold, you fool?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:06.63,0:26:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.61,0:26:11.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll see you two, chips, sir,\Nand hear all six Polnareffs.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.11,0:26:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,And, for laughs,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.83,0:26:15.83,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm raising your six Josephs!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:16.29,0:26:19.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That's fifteen chips in\Nall! What? Wait a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:19.75,0:26:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro has no more chips\Nleft to call your bet.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.29,0:26:23.27,Default,,0,0,0,,No more chips?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.47,0:26:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He still has some. What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:25.93,0:26:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, now, all he needs to do is write\Nme out a little old promisorite note.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.81,0:26:33.09,Default,,0,0,0,,That's just as good as gold as\Nfar as my stand is concerned.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:33.17,0:26:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Like I said, what are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.83,0:26:39.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Why he can bet the soul of his friend\NKakyoin, who's hospitalized in Aswa.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:39.97,0:26:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.41,0:26:44.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on boys, start sweating.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:44.53,0:26:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare you try to bluff me, Darby.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.05,0:26:50.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll turn that poker face of\Nyours into a mask of fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.09,0:26:52.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Then it's agreed.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.17,0:26:54.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll raise you all of Kakyoin's soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.31,0:26:58.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro, that soul belongs\Nto someone who's not here.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.55,0:26:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Am I being selfish?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:59.89,0:27:02.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey Jotaro, what you trying to pull?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.31,0:27:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.65,0:27:04.65,Default,,0,0,0,,What did I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.95,0:27:05.95,Default,,0,0,0,,That smoke there?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.35,0:27:08.41,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.55,0:27:09.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you feeling sick?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.05,0:27:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did that cigarette\Ncome from just now?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:12.85,0:27:14.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought I saw Star Platinum light it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:14.77,0:27:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What confidence could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.31,0:27:20.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Did Star Platinum switch those\Ncards without me noticing?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:20.43,0:27:22.89,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I was watching his cards carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.97,0:27:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't see the cigarette only\Nbecause I was concentrating.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:25.63,0:27:26.46,Default,,0,0,0,,On his cards
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.54,0:27:33.45,Default,,0,0,0,,four
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.27,0:27:35.10,Default,,0,0,0,,of a
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.18,0:27:36.08,Default,,0,0,0,,kind with kings to have
Dialogue: 0,0:27:36.17,0:27:38.70,Default,,0,0,0,,a better hand than this\Nhe'd need four of a
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.69,0:27:43.55,Default,,0,0,0,,kind with aces, a straight flush,\Nor five of a kind with the joker.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.63,0:27:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro's cards are rags.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.67,0:27:49.93,Default,,0,0,0,,For him to make a good hand, he would\Nhave needed to switch all five cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.01,0:27:52.51,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter how vast Star Platinum may be,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.87,0:27:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,is it really possible that he could have\Nswitched not one, but all five cards
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.05,0:27:59.01,Default,,0,0,0,,without attracting my\Nattention in the slightest?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.09,0:28:00.03,Default,,0,0,0,,It can't be.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.15,0:28:00.98,Default,,0,0,0,,It's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.06,0:28:03.18,Default,,0,0,0,,There is absolutely no way\Nhe could have switched all
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.27,0:28:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,five cards without a veteran\Ngambler like me noticing
Dialogue: 0,0:28:06.63,0:28:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,in something.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.54,0:28:08.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Alrighty then, Jotaro.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.57,0:28:09.73,Default,,0,0,0,,You want a showdown?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:09.81,0:28:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll give you one.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.35,0:28:14.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Try to pull a useless bluff on\Nme with that stupid cigarette.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:15.33,0:28:16.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.99,0:28:19.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You got yourself a treat now?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.41,0:28:21.57,Default,,0,0,0,,When did you...
Dialogue: 0,0:28:21.65,0:28:23.59,Default,,0,0,0,,How dare you?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.39,0:28:26.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, showdown. Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:26.87,0:28:27.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.07,0:28:30.45,Default,,0,0,0,,There's the little matter\Nof a raise I'd like to make.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:30.53,0:28:31.36,Default,,0,0,0,,What the?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:32.01,0:28:32.93,Default,,0,0,0,,You're raising?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.49,0:28:34.90,Default,,0,0,0,,But you're out of chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.03,0:28:35.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna
Dialogue: 0,0:28:38.87,0:28:39.70,Default,,0,0,0,,raise you.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:39.78,0:28:41.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm gonna raise you my mother's soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:42.85,0:28:43.68,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:43.76,0:28:44.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Your mother's?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.67,0:28:46.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro, not Miss Holly's soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.07,0:28:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I came here to Egypt for one\Nreason, to save my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:50.63,0:28:52.45,Default,,0,0,0,,So she would have no objections
Dialogue: 0,0:28:52.95,0:28:55.77,Default,,0,0,0,,whatsoever for me to bet\Nthe six chips of her soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:55.85,0:28:56.68,Default,,0,0,0,,But Darby,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.87,0:28:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to ask you to see Be my bet with
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.41,0:29:02.35,Default,,0,0,0,,something that's equal in\Nvalue to my mother-soul.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.23,0:29:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,If you lose, you have to reveal\Nthe secret of Dio's stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.65,0:29:18.59,Default,,0,0,0,,That reaction? He knows.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:18.77,0:29:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,He knows Dio's secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:20.17,0:29:22.52,Default,,0,0,0,,But if Darby talks, he'll lose his life.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.65,0:29:24.18,Default,,0,0,0,,A traitor would be killed!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:28.73,0:29:31.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Your confidence must mean\Nyou have a winning hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.67,0:29:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it really all right to assume that?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.95,0:29:36.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Those cards will surely\Nwin, right, Jotaro?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:38.59,0:29:41.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, are you going to call or fold?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.49,0:29:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Say it out loud right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.15,0:29:44.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Darby!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:00.99,0:30:06.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Honestly, I'm the greatest.\NI've got to accept you, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:08.77,0:30:10.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.23,0:30:29.06,Default,,0,0,0,,That...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:29.14,0:30:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,that man just...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.13,0:30:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong with him?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:34.59,0:30:35.87,Default,,0,0,0,,He passed out.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.49,0:30:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,The two souls! They're saved!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.37,0:30:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,He must have passed out\Nfrom too much tension.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.57,0:30:57.17,Default,,0,0,0,,He conceded the game.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:57.43,0:30:59.49,Default,,0,0,0,,In his mind, he'd folded the cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:59.75,0:31:04.40,Default,,0,0,0,,So all the souls he captured are now\Nreleased since he has admitted his defeat.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:05.89,0:31:07.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Four of a kind!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:07.27,0:31:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,In his hand, he had four kings!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.81,0:31:13.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro, those face-down cards\Nof yours, what were they?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.45,0:31:19.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, I thought so!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.51,0:31:20.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing but garbage!
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.71,0:31:24.97,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter how quick Star Platinum is,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:25.19,0:31:28.37,Default,,0,0,0,,there's no way I could have\Ncheated around a man like Darby.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.45,0:31:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,My plan was to get him\Nto be scared and fold.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:31.07,0:31:34.66,Default,,0,0,0,,I would have freaked out if I'd\Nknown I had this crappy hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.15,0:31:35.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Freaked out?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:36.25,0:31:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Jotaro, I can't believe you took\Nsuch a chance on those lousy cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.13,0:31:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,By the way, kid, you\Njust said I thought so.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:45.21,0:31:47.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Does that mean you knew\Nwhat my cards were?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:57.71,0:31:58.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, everyone!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.43,0:32:02.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's play Macho.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.03,0:32:04.68,Default,,0,0,0,,That coming is a lot of fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:05.85,0:32:07.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Dice is thrilling too.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:08.07,0:32:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,No matter what, I'm always the best.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:10.31,0:32:12.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, now tell us, where's that mansion?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.51,0:32:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Old Cairo, where the\Nwhorehouse used to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.11,0:32:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Dio, stand.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.25,0:32:18.37,Default,,0,0,0,,What is its secret?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:18.93,0:32:20.19,Default,,0,0,0,,No. No!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.03,0:32:24.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The way he is now.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.85,0:32:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I do not think we will ever\Nget Dio's secret out of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.03,0:32:29.65,Default,,0,0,0,,He was definitely formidable.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:29.73,0:32:32.41,Default,,0,0,0,,He tried to defeat all\Nfour of us by himself.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.73,0:32:34.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That's pretty impressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.89,0:32:42.27,Default,,0,0,0,,At any rate, I'd say we're lucky to have\Nfound out the location of the mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.35,0:32:44.53,Default,,0,0,0,,We don't have any more time to waste.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.31,0:33:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,VINCIROR
Dialogue: 0,0:33:31.27,0:33:35.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Vincero. Vincero.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.85,0:33:40.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Vincero.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:43.13,0:33:44.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Vincero.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:53.87,0:33:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I love you. I love
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.33,0:34:03.33,Default,,0,0,0,,you?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.07,0:36:16.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
